 ## 2026-08-27
 
+### 0625 — Physical HEV/bridge matrix meets the provisional incremental target (TASK-260715-135rr8)
+- MEASUREMENT: A physical Mac15,9 (arm64, macOS 26.5) SwiftPM run admitted 100, 250, and the explicitly narrowed 500-session ceiling with zero bridge drops. Physical footprint was 12,354,160 B, 15,270,512 B, and 20,038,256 B; peak was 20,054,640 B. The incremental 500-session HEV/bridge cost was 11,976,704 B, leaving 19,480,576 B inside the provisional 30 MiB envelope. This is not a whole-extension Apple guarantee and does not allocate SSH, DNS, relay, caches, or reconnect overlap.
+- LIFECYCLE: One hundred real HEV start/traffic/stop cycles restored descriptors, sessions, queued batches, outstanding reads, boundary start/stop ownership, and HEV/bridge close stages; sampled physical footprint did not grow monotonically. Seven startup and seven cleanup cancellation stages plus 50 harness host-termination iterations passed.
+- AVAILABILITY: `os_proc_available_memory` is explicitly unavailable on macOS in the public SDK. HEV queued bytes and process-wide Swift task counts also have no public gauge. All are recorded as unavailable/unknown; host memory, process threads, and proxy zeros were not substituted. Physical iPhone and sleep/wake remain named deferred gaps.
+- PRESSURE: Real stalled-path pressure accounts every send or bounded drop and cleans up. Soft/pressure/critical ordering remains deferred until SSH admission integration because the current memory-pressure seam is advisory and has no production policy consumer; no global pressure tool was invoked.
+- VERIFICATION: The full Swift suite and full coverage suite each passed 480 tests in 40 suites with 25 declared known candidate-unavailable issues. Affected coverage is 84.84% regions, 96.02% functions, and 93.09% lines. Strict affected-file format lint and `git diff --check` pass. Raw matrix JSON and logs are attached as task-scoped evidence.
+
 ### 2356 — Physical macOS MTU/socket baseline separates queue drops from send refusal (TASK-260715-gyg51r)
 - MEASUREMENT: The bounded loopback-only SPM harness ran 36 rows on a physical Apple M3 Max Mac (arm64, macOS 26.5): MTU 1500/4096/8500 × IPv4/native IPv6/dual stack × nominal/constrained-buffer/25ms receiver-stall/mixed bidirectional traffic. Nominal and mixed rows delivered 100%; pressure rows produced only named bounded effects and recovered with zero production-owned descriptor delta. Swift-task delta is explicitly unavailable because the synchronous runner owns no tasks; process threads are not treated as a proxy.
 - FINDING: Requested/effective buffers matched at 4096, 32768, and 262144 bytes. MTU 8500 with a 4096-byte send buffer produced 768 errno-40 `Message too long` refusals across the three family rows plus receive-queue drops; its maximum successful constrained datagram was 768 bytes. This is distinct from receiver overflow and makes 8500 unsuitable as a default solely because upstream uses it.
